# Environment
.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Data directory (too large for GitHub — regenerate via scripts/update_data.py)
/data/

# Trained models — sub-model folders ignored, production model tracked in git
/models/GRU/
/models/LSTM/
/models/RF/
/models/XGBoost/
/models/scalers/

# Legacy notebooks (all logic migrated to src/)
/notebooks/

# Secret-bearing variants — .env alone does not cover these
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local.yaml
*.local.json
secrets.json
credentials.json
*.pem
*.key

# Local working notes — never committed. These accumulate personal context
# and operational detail (server access, deployment specifics) that does not
# belong in a repository.
/*.md
!README.md

# Optuna tuning artifacts. The chosen hyperparameters ARE committed
# (results/tuning/xgboost_best_params_v2.json — train_production.py and the
# weekly monitor both read it, so the pipeline breaks without it). These are
# the raw search byproducts: binary study databases and per-trial logs, worth
# hundreds of KB, regenerable by re-running scripts/tune_xgboost.py, and of no
# use to anyone reading the repo.
results/tuning/*.db
results/tuning/xgboost_tuning_results*.csv

# Superseded v1 tuning output, kept locally for reference only.
results/tuning/xgboost_best_params.json

# One-off local diagram, not referenced by the app or any script.
pipeline_diagram.html

